# ── build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Everything below is computed by `npm run build:data` from content/ and data/,
# and none of it is worth reviewing, diffing or committing. It used to be: 4002
# files and 28.7 MB of generated JSON in git, so a single new reading arrived as
# 133 lines of authored YAML plus 575 lines of readings.json and two whole-file
# rewrites of minified payloads. Nobody read those diffs, and two sessions
# authoring at once conflicted on files neither had edited.
#
# CI runs the same chain before deploying (.github/workflows/deploy.yml), and it
# already builds the vidyut WASM that build:quiz needs — measured at 13s, which
# is why the expensive step can run there rather than being carried in the repo.
#
# See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. If you add a generated file, add it here too, or it
# will be committed and start rotting the moment its source changes.

static/data/readings.json
static/data/usage.json
static/data/quiz-cells.json
static/data/tin-forms.json
static/data/sutras.json
static/data/sutra-refs/
static/data/readings-by-sutra.json
static/data/balabodhini.json
static/data/jargon.json
static/data/dhatu-map.json
static/data/stats.json
static/data/commentary-index.json

# NOT ignored, and each for a reason the cold-build test found:
#
#   vocabulary.json          authored. build-quiz READS it for gender hints and
#                            never writes it — the 42-entry lexicon is source.
#   dukrnkarane.json         imported from a sibling repository.
#   dukrnkarane-by-sutra.json  build-dukrnkarane.ts reads a checkout of the
#   sutrartha_english.json     dukrnkarane project ($DUKR_SRC) and skips with a
#                            notice when it is absent, keeping the committed
#                            payload. Not reproducible here, so not ignorable
#                            here — they are vendored, not generated.
#
# The invariant to preserve: everything ignored above can be rebuilt by
# `npm run build:data` from a clean checkout. Verify with
#   git clean -Xfd static/data static/content && npm run build:data
static/content/paths-index.json
static/content/sutra-paths.json
